{"name":"Sandy Bay","hex":"#fad7b3","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Sandy Bay","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A bay in Pok Fu Lam, Southern district, Hong Kong.","A suburb of the City of Hobart, Tasmania, Australia."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Sandy_Bay"}],"entries":[{"title":"Sandy Bay, Cape Town","blocks":[{"text":"Sandy Bay is a beach just south of Llandudno. It is on the west side of the Karbonkelberg, and cannot be seen from the main road to Hout Bay, which turns inland above Llandudno."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/56/Sandy_Bay%2C_Cape_Town.jpg/330px-Sandy_Bay%2C_Cape_Town.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sandy_Bay%2C_Cape_Town","wikidata":"Q7417149"},{"title":"Sandy Bay, Saint Helena","blocks":[{"text":"Sandy Bay is one of eight districts of the island of Saint Helena, part of the British Overseas Territory of Saint Helena, Ascension and Tristan da Cunha in the South Atlantic Ocean. Located on the island's southeastern coast, it is sparsely populated and is a popular recreation site."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6e/View_of_Sandy_Bay_Saint_Helena.jpg/330px-View_of_Sandy_Bay_Saint_Helena.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sandy_Bay%2C_Saint_Helena","wikidata":"Q7417151"},{"title":"Bay","blocks":[{"text":"A bay is a recessed, coastal body of water that directly connects to a larger main body of water, such as an ocean, a lake, or another bay. A large bay is usually called a gulf, sea, sound, or bight. A cove is a small, circular bay with a narrow entrance. A fjord is an elongated bay formed by glacial action.\nThe term embayment is also used for related features, such as extinct bays or freshwater environments."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f1/Aerial_photograph_of_Langness_and_the_bay_at_Castletown_13_February_2014_-_geograph.org.uk_-_3847162.jpg/330px-Aerial_photograph_of_Langness_and_the_bay_at_Castletown_13_February_2014_-_geograph.org.uk_-_3847162.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bay","wikidata":"Q39594"},{"title":"Bay (horse)","blocks":[{"text":"Bay is a hair coat color of horses, characterized by a reddish-brown or brown body color with a black point coloration on the mane, tail, ear edges, and lower legs. Bay is one of the most common coat colors in many horse breeds."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/ca/BayMare.jpg/330px-BayMare.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bay_(horse)","wikidata":"Q900906"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bf/Lot%27s_Wife%27s_Ponds_in_Sandy_Bay_Saint_Helena.jpg/500px-Lot%27s_Wife%27s_Ponds_in_Sandy_Bay_Saint_Helena.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bf/Lot%27s_Wife%27s_Ponds_in_Sandy_Bay_Saint_Helena.jpg/1280px-Lot%27s_Wife%27s_Ponds_in_Sandy_Bay_Saint_Helena.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bf/Lot%27s_Wife%27s_Ponds_in_Sandy_Bay_Saint_Helena.jpg/500px-Lot%27s_Wife%27s_Ponds_in_Sandy_Bay_Saint_Helena.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Lot's Wife's Ponds","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ALot's_Wife's_Ponds_in_Sandy_Bay_Saint_Helena.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8a/Baptist_chapel_in_Sandy_Bay.jpg/120px-Baptist_chapel_in_Sandy_Bay.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/common